[size=5][b]Fus-Perkele-Dah![/b] A Finnish summer in Skyrim.[/size]

[youtube]IJzDb4E7bYA[/youtube]

[url=https://discord.gg/C687NV4dCp]Discord[/url] · [url=https://github.com/rackmarten/PerkeleRim]Source on GitHub[/url] · [url=https://ko-fi.com/rackmarten]Buy Kumpo a beer[/url][/center]

[line]

[b]My Summer Car[/b] and [b]Skyrim (Special or Anniversary Edition)[/b] run at the same time. Skyrim owns the world and draws everything; My Summer Car runs hidden and simulates Kumpo, the vehicles, the beer and the piss. Drive the Hayosiko van across the Whiterun tundra, get drunk, punch a Thalmor, and take the Kekmet tractor up the Throat of the World.

[b]v0.1.1.[/b] It's playable start to finish, but it's young: expect bugs, and please report them (see below).

[size=4][b]What you get[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The Hayosiko van, the Jonnez moped and the Kekmet tractor on Skyrim's roads, with working doors, gauges, lights and radio
[*]A garage on the tundra south-west of Whiterun, where your first drive starts
[*]MSC's needs (thirst, hunger, stress, urine, fatigue, drunkenness) in Skyrim's HUD
[*]Mead and ale picked up in Skyrim become MSC beer. The drunker Kumpo is, the harder he hits
[*]Fist fights with Skyrim's people, thrown bottles as a ranged attack, piss as poison, and running people over
[*]Unrelenting Force, yelled by Kumpo: "Perkele!"
[*]Skyrim saves keep MSC's state, vehicles included
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Windows 10/11 and a PC that can run both games at once
[*][url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/489830/]Skyrim Special Edition or Anniversary Edition[/url] (latest Steam version, or Special Edition 1.5.97) with [url=https://skse.silverlock.org]SKSE64[/url] for that version and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url] (the "Special Edition" file on 1.5.97, "All in one (Anniversary Edition)" otherwise)
[*][url=https://store.steampowered.com/app/516750/]My Summer Car[/url] (Steam) with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mysummercar/mods/147]MSCLoader[/url]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Install and play[/b][/size]
Install manually, not with a mod manager.
[list=1]
[*]Download the main file and extract it anywhere (not inside a game folder).
[*]Double-click [b]Start PerkeleRim.bat[/b]. It finds both games, checks for SKSE, Address Library and MSCLoader, installs or updates the mod, and starts both games (My Summer Car minimizes itself).
[*]Play in Skyrim only. Load the [b]PerkeleRim-Kumpo[/b] save (Anniversary Edition only; on Special Edition start a new game or load your own) and press [b]F10[/b] to hand over to My Summer Car. Leave MSC minimized.
[/list]

[spoiler]
Every time you run Start PerkeleRim.bat, it:
[list]
[*]finds both games in your Steam libraries, or asks for their folders once (saved in PerkeleRim.ini next to it; delete that file to look again)
[*]tells you if SKSE, Address Library or MSCLoader is missing
[*]installs or updates the mod (the SKSE plugin and PerkeleRim.esp in Skyrim, enabled in plugins.txt; the MSCLoader mod where MSCLoader keeps mods)
[*]gives My Summer Car a starter save when you have none, never over yours
[*]adds a starter Skyrim save, PerkeleRim-Kumpo (a male Nord just out of Helgen, before his first F10), next to your own saves, never over one (Anniversary Edition only: Special Edition 1.5.97 can't load it)
[*]starts My Summer Car in a small window that minimizes itself and continues your MSC save, then starts Skyrim through SKSE
[/list]
[/spoiler]

Playing your own character? Make him a male Nord, like the starter save's Kumpo. While MSC has the player, Skyrim's own voice is muted and Kumpo Kempolaari (Finn) does the yelling, grunting and swearing, so a Nord fits best whenever Skyrim has the player back.

[line]

[size=4][b]Keys[/b][/size]
F10 hands the player to My Summer Car and back. While MSC has the player you never need its window: WASD and the mouse are MSC's, Skyrim keeps Escape (pauses both games), Tab, M (map), F5/F9 and the console.
[list]
[*][b]Left / right click[/b] (free hands): punch / guard
[*][b]V[/b]: middle finger
[*][b]Z[/b]: Skyrim's shout or power, yelled by Kumpo
[*][b]Alt[/b] (tap): piss until empty
[*][b]Middle click[/b]: swear
[*][b]C / B[/b]: smoke / zoom
[*][b]Ctrl / G[/b] (on foot): crouch / push stance (shove people aside, right a rolled van)
[*][b]O[/b]: hitchhike thumb
[*][b]T[/b] (on foot): Skyrim's Wait menu; MSC's clock and needs go along
[*][b]Shift / Ctrl[/b] (driving): shift up / down
[*][b]H[/b] (driving): horn, people in the way run off
[*][b]F8[/b] (driving): chase camera for filming
[*][b]F11[/b]: screenshot of both games
[*][b][ / ] / ;[/b] (on foot): call the moped / the van / the Kekmet to you
[*][b]Y, 3 to 8[/b]: the pocket (Skyrim's inventory) for beer, bottles, food and cigarettes
[/list]
Full key list: [url=https://github.com/rackmarten/PerkeleRim#keys]GitHub README[/url].

Kumpo fights with his fists: weapons and spells can't be equipped while MSC has the player, armor works as usual. Sitting in the van or the Kekmet is safe: nothing in Skyrim can hurt Kumpo there (the moped is no shelter, and a crash still hurts).

[line]

[size=4][b]Known issues[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Followers get in the way and are easy to run over. Don't take one along in v0.1.
[*]Horses don't work properly, so don't ride them. Kumpo is a drunk, not a horse rider.
[*]Water is mostly ignored: Kumpo walks on the bottom and vehicles drive through it. Wading in up to the waist still washes him.
[*]Vehicles have no hitbox in Skyrim, so arrows and dragons pass through the van.
[/list]

