[*]Water and swimming
[/list]
Later, maybe: the Gifu and delivery jobs, more Finnish summer (sauna, bright evenings), one wallet for MSC money and Skyrim gold. Tell us what you'd enjoy in #perkelerim-ideas on [url=https://discord.gg/C687NV4dCp]Discord[/url].

[line]

[size=4][b]Bugs and feedback[/b][/size]
Double-click [b]Report a bug.bat[/b] (next to Start PerkeleRim.bat). It zips your PerkeleRim logs from both games and opens the bug form on GitHub with the versions filled in. Nothing is sent anywhere until you submit it, and PerkeleRim has no telemetry. You can also post in the Bugs tab here or on [url=https://discord.gg/C687NV4dCp]Discord[/url].

[size=4][b]How it works[/b][/size]
An SKSE plugin (C++) samples Skyrim's collision around the player and draws the MSC player, vehicles and items inside Skyrim. An MSCLoader mod (C#) builds that collision inside My Summer Car and runs the physics on it. The two talk over shared memory. No assets from either game are shipped: Skyrim draws MSC's van and items from your own running copy of My Summer Car. Open source under MIT, on [url=https://github.com/rackmarten/PerkeleRim]GitHub[/url].

Inspired by [url=https://github.com/chasmlol/SkyCraft]SkyCraft[/url], which couples Minecraft and Skyrim the same way.

